  "initialFailuresAndCorrections": [
    "Initial SQL approval fixture lacked registered account-control keys; exact owned audit FK cleanup and random Telegram fixture identities were corrected. SQL verification then passed 11 cases.",
    "Initial complete core/frontend/modules and broader browser runs correctly refused incomplete or mismatched 18/25/MCP/starter cohorts. New immutable artifacts and exact peer/range tests were prepared; none of the consumed archives or historical fixtures was overwritten.",
    "An email browser waiter matched the wrong proxy URL. It now matches the canonical pathname and proves actual email-code login and in-card renewal.",
    "The first expanded client integration passed 83/84; a post-OAuth Codex thread refused the membership token. Unique server names and a fresh ephemeral read-only thread after reload resolved the harness state issue. No inference or product transport change was introduced.",
    "The first clean frontend command used the wrong API environment flag; overlapping builds were discarded and a final serial VITE_NETWORK=testnet/VITE_API_TESTNET build supplies the published entry.",
    "The first API18 startup was refused by the exact-version recovery gate. API17/frontend22 were restored successfully before fresh synthetic TLS restore and configured live roundtrip. A new report retains the original expiry; the gate was not weakened.",
    "After the SDK bump, inspection found that preserving the old active starter would fail MINI_APP_RELEASE_VERSION. The corrected deployment selects starter18/25 and explicitly retains old17/24 downloads. RED archived download returned 404; final integration covers current configuration, version refusal, old bytes/ETags, unknown IDs, duplicate/bounded archives and tamper refusal.",
    "The first ad hoc public catalog probe attempted JSON parsing on a valid SSE response. Its parser now handles both JSON and SSE; final nine downloads/catalog/authentication checks passed. Actual Codex and Claude public clients had already succeeded.",
    "Existing frontend chunk-size warnings remain. No unrelated bundling or dependency change was added."
  ],
